From: Dustin Kirkland <dustin.kirkland@chainguard.dev>
Subject: universal: fall back to pdftoraster when built without Ghostscript

The PDF -> raster branch of cfFilterUniversal() sat entirely inside
#if defined(HAVE_GHOSTSCRIPT), so a --disable-ghostscript build could
not produce PWG/URF/CUPS raster or PCLm at all ("Output format is not
PDF and unknown") and its pdftoraster (pdftoppm) fallback was dead
code. Keep the branch unconditional: Ghostscript when built in,
otherwise pdftoraster.
---
diff --git a/cupsfilters/universal.c b/cupsfilters/universal.c
index 6948874..0161e1e 100644
--- a/cupsfilters/universal.c
+++ b/cupsfilters/universal.c
@@ -270,7 +270,11 @@ cfFilterUniversal(int inputfd,		// I - File descriptor input stream
 		     "cfFilterUniversal: Adding %s to chain", filter->name);
       }
 
-#if defined(HAVE_GHOSTSCRIPT)
+      // PDF -> raster: Ghostscript when built in, otherwise pdftoraster
+      // (poppler's pdftoppm). The raster branch used to sit entirely inside
+      // HAVE_GHOSTSCRIPT, so a build without Ghostscript could not produce
+      // PWG/URF/CUPS raster or PCLm at all and the pdftoraster fallback below
+      // was dead code.
       if (strcasecmp(output_type, "vnd.cups-pdf"))
       {
 	if (!strcasecmp(output_type, "vnd.cups-raster") ||
@@ -320,14 +324,11 @@ cfFilterUniversal(int inputfd,		// I - File descriptor input stream
 	}
 	else
 	{
-#endif // HAVE_GHOSTSCRIPT
 	  // Output format is not PDF and unknown -> Error
 	  ret = 1;
 	  goto out;
-#if defined(HAVE_GHOSTSCRIPT)
 	}
       }
-#endif // HAVE_GHOSTSCRIPT
     }
   }
 
